'''acroasis''' (ak-rọ̄-ā′sis), ''n.'' [L., < Gr. ἀκρόασις, a hearing or lecture, < ἀκροᾶσθαι, hear: see ''acroama''.] An oral discourse.

'''acroatic''' (ak-rọ̄-at′ik), ''a.'' [< L. ''acroaticus'', < Gr. ἀκροατικός, of or for hearing, < ἀκροατής, a hearer, < ἀκροᾶσθαι, hear: see ''acroama''.] Same as ''acroamatic''.

'''acroatics''' (ak-rọ̄-at′iks), ''n. pl.'' Same as ''acroamatics''.

