'''acrobat''' (ak′rọ̄-bat), ''n.'' [< F. ''acrobate'' = Sp. ''acróbato'' = Pg. It. ''acrobata'' (cf. NL. ''Acrobates''), < Gr. ἀκρόβατος, walking on tiptoe, also going to the top, < ἄκρον, the highest point, top, summit, neut. of ἄκρος, highest, topmost, + βατός, verbal
