'''Acrobates''' (ak-rob′a̤-tēz), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. as if *ἀκροβάτης, equiv. to ἀκρόβατος: see ''acrobat''.] A genus or subgenus of marsupial quadrupeds of the family ''Phalangistidæ'', peculiar to Australia. {{smaller|It is related to ''Petaurus'', and includes such pygmy petaurists as the opossum-mouse, ''Acro-''}}

